  "name": null,
  "problem": "The time it takes John to get to school, in minutes, is normally distributed with a mean of $20\\,\\text{min}$ and a standard deviation of $6\\,\\text{min}.$\nWhat is the probability that the sum of the times John takes to get to school on $5$ randomly selected school days is more than $90\\,\\text{min}?$\nYou may assume that the times of each day are mutually independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
